---
{
  title: "map_async"
}
---
### NAME

    map_async() - Applies an async function to every element of an array at
    once and collects the results.

### SYNOPSIS

    async varargs mixed *map_async( mixed *src, function fun, mixed extra... );

### DESCRIPTION

    Applies an async function to every element of an array at once and
    collects the results.

    The fan-out counterpart to each_async(): where that one visits elements
    in order and waits for each before starting the next, this starts them
    all and then waits for the set. Use it when the elements do not depend
    on each other and the waiting is what costs — a batch of file listings,
    a batch of requests. For work that is expensive to *run* rather than to
    wait for, each_async() is still the right shape, because starting a
    thousand pieces of computation at once does not make the driver compute
    them any faster.

    The callback is called with (element, index, array, ...extra), as each()
    and each_async() call it. Results are positional: entry i is what the
    callback returned for src[i], whatever order the calls settled in. A
    callback that is not async contributes its plain return value, so a
    mixed batch works.

    The first rejection rejects the whole thing, and the calls already
    running are not stopped — nothing here cancels anything. When a partial
    failure is a result rather than an error, reach for settle_async()
    instead.

    Every element is started before any of them is judged, including past
    one that fails. A synchronous callback can throw where an async one
    would only reject; that counts as its own element rejecting and nothing
    more.

    The fan-out is unbounded: every element holds a suspended frame until
    the set settles, so slice a large array into batches rather than handing
    the whole thing over at once.

### PARAMETERS

    src    (mixed *)
           Array to fan out over.

    fun    (function)
           Function called per element (see above).

    extra  (mixed, optional)
           Additional arguments passed to the callback starting at $4.

### RETURN VALUES

    (mixed *) A promise for the results, positionally matching src.

### ERRORS

    If src is not an array, or fun is not a valid function. Either rejects
    the returned promise.

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}string **listings = await map_async(dirs, (: async_getdir($1) :));{{di0}}
